      {
        "title": "Smog Dog",
        "text": "Smog Dog, from Skitchin's CD Player, plays its melody on the PSG, the square-wave chip in the Genesis. The songs for San Diego, Seattle, Toronto and Chicago do the same."
      },
      {
        "picture": "../_games/skitchin/jeff-van-dyck.png",
        "caption": "Jeff van Dyck"
      },
      {
        "title": "From CD quality to 8 bits",
        "text": "Composer Jeff van Dyck wrote the songs for Skitchin' on a Mac, using MOTU Performer and CD-quality samples on a SampleCell card. To fit them on the cartridge, the guitars and drums were cut down to 11 kHz, mono, 8-bit. In this player they run at the game's own rate of 11,331 Hz."
      }
    ]
